Young Syd developed his baseball skills playing in sandlot teams in El Paso’s Boyland League where he played third base, catcher, right field, and pitcher. Describing the grammar school league, the El Paso Hearld [, describing Grammar School league,] mentioned that Cohen's "has some curves which would make bigger boys jealous"  A left-handed thrower and a switch-hitter, Syd eventually grew to 5-foot-11, 180 pounds.
